<p class="lead">We respect the work of authors, teachers and students. If something on this site belongs to you and should not be here, tell us and we will review it quickly.</p>

<h2>Who owns what</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The site.</strong> The DIU StudyHub name, logo, design and code are &copy; <%= year %> <%= SITE.owner %>. All rights reserved.</li>
  <li><strong>Shared files.</strong> Files on the site belong to their original authors or rights holders. Uploading a file does not transfer ownership to DIU StudyHub.</li>
  <li><strong>Daffodil International University.</strong> The university's name is used only to describe who the site is for. The site is not affiliated with or endorsed by the university.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Asking us to remove a file</h2>
<p>If you are the copyright owner, or act for the owner, send us a message through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> that includes:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Your name and a way to reach you</li>
  <li>The address (URL) of the file page on DIU StudyHub</li>
  <li>A description of the work that you say has been copied</li>
  <li>A statement that you are the rights holder or are allowed to act for them</li>
  <li>A statement that the information in your message is accurate</li>
</ol>
<p>We will review the request promptly and remove the file where the claim appears valid. We may contact the uploader about it.</p>

<h2>If your file was removed by mistake</h2>
<p>Uploaders who believe a removal was a mistake can contact us with the file name and an explanation of why they have the right to share it. We will take another look.</p>

<h2>Repeat problems</h2>
<p>Accounts that repeatedly upload material they do not have the right to share may be suspended.</p>

<h2>Uploaders, please remember</h2>
<p>Only share what you created or are allowed to share. Teacher-provided slides and past exam questions are commonly shared inside the university community, but full commercial textbooks are not welcome. See the <a href="/guidelines">upload guidelines</a>.</p>
